# Sustainable Fashion Research Plan Revision Update Improvements<br>
<br>
## Introduction<br>
<br>
As part of our ongoing efforts to create sustainable fashion designs, I have revised the research plan to include more specific examples of sustainable textile patterns and colors.<br>
<br>
## Textile Patterns<br>
<br>
* Natural dyes such as indigo, turmeric, and pomegranate can be used to create unique and sustainable patterns.<br>
* Organic cotton and hemp fabrics can be woven into intricate patterns that reduce waste and promote sustainability.<br>
<br>
## Colors<br>
<br>
* Earthy tones such as olive green, terracotta, and sandy beige can be used to create a natural and sustainable color palette.<br>
* Blues and greens can also be used to represent the ocean and environment.<br>
<br>
## Incorporating Sustainable Elements into Designs<br>
<br>
* Use natural dyes and organic cotton/hemp fabrics in designs to reduce waste and promote sustainability.<br>
* Incorporate earthy tones and blues/greens into designs to create a natural and sustainable color palette.<br>
<br>
